  "id": "DrugBank_DB01029 - MONDO_5044",
  "verbalization": "Irbesartan is implicated in the pathogenesis of Hypertensive Disorder through a chain of indications that connect it to Diabetic Nephropathy, which in turn links to Captopril and Losartan. The evidence suggests that Irbesartan may exert a therapeutic effect on Hypertensive Disorder via a mechanism that involves the treatment of Diabetic Nephropathy, a condition often associated with hypertension. The indirect pathway through Captopril, a drug known to treat hypertension, further supports the notion that Irbesartan's role in Hypertensive Disorder may be mediated through its effects on Diabetic Nephropathy. The overlapping indications highlight a potential mechanistic link, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering comorbid conditions in the context of drug repurposing.",
